d class (i.e. race, sex, religion), Personal use.", "access_policy": "All system access requires a valid reason.", "hotlist_policy": "Hotlist hits are required to be human verified prior to action.", "page_name": "Auburn WA PD", "portal_status": "active", "portal_last_updated": "2026-06-27T18:05:37.259Z", "more_info": {"Network Sharing Policy": "We share statewide only.", "Recent Success Story": "In the spring of 2025, Auburn Police responded to a call for service which resulted in a homicide investigation. During the investigation, APD personnel learned that a specific vehicle was used by the suspects to flee the scene. Using city owned camera footage, APD personnel managed to obtain some video of the suspect vehicle, but the clarity was limited, only allowing APD personnel to gather a general description of its make and model.\n\nHowever, when APD personnel searched the Flock Safety Camera system in our city, a matching make and model was quickly located, which provided APD with a license plate number. By combining the information from the city owned camera systems with Flock, APD personnel were able to confirm the exact vehicle involved in the homicide. Within six hours, APD personnel entered the license plate into a WA State system as a Be On the Look Out (BOLO) for the awareness of all law enforcement.\n\nLater that day, an officer from an outside agency found the suspect vehicle abandoned on the side of the road. Thanks to the quick identification of the vehicle, APD personnel were able to collect very valuable evidence. This success would not have been possible without Flock. The suspect in the homicide was later arrested and booked into jail."}}
